\details{
\code{analyze_eap_power_sensitivity()} recomputes fixed-calibration EAP summaries
under a grid of power-scaled posterior weights,
\code{prior_weight ^ prior_power * likelihood ^ likelihood_power}, after
evaluating the existing response likelihood on the fitted quadrature grid.
The fitted item/facet calibration is not refit.

This is a lightweight scoring diagnostic inspired by Bayesian
power-scaling sensitivity analysis. It is deliberately narrower than
\code{priorsense}-style workflows: no MCMC draws, Pareto-smoothed importance
sampling, moment matching, or posterior-refit diagnostics are used. Because
the current scoring posterior is already represented on a finite quadrature
grid, the package can directly renormalize the perturbed grid weights and
report how EAP summaries change from the reference condition.

For ordinary \code{MML} fits, the reference prior is the fitted normal
quadrature prior: fixed by \code{population_prior_sd} or estimated through
\code{estimate_population_sd = TRUE}. For latent-regression \code{MML} fits, the
power is applied to the fitted conditional-normal quadrature weights for
each scored person. For \code{JML} fits, the function uses the same post hoc
standard-normal reference prior used by \code{\link[=predict_mfrm_units]{predict_mfrm_units()}}.
}
\section{Interpreting output}{

\itemize{
\item \code{sensitivity} contains one row per person per power condition, including
deltas from the unscaled reference EAP and posterior SD.
\item \code{summary} aggregates the absolute and signed deltas by power condition.
\item \code{facet_stability} and \code{facet_overview} aggregate person-level deltas over
the facet levels appearing in \code{new_data}; these are exposure-weighted
diagnostic summaries, not causal decompositions of item/rater effects.
\item Large \code{DeltaEstimate} or \code{DeltaSD} values indicate that reported EAP
scores are sensitive to the scoring prior/likelihood balance under the
